  "title": "Kafka: Sanity check array dissection",
  "description": "Validate that array counts are reasonable - assuming 1 byte per array item, ensure the array still fits in the remaining packet data. Also validate that dissecting an array item advances the offset.\n\nThese sanity checks fix an issue with fuzzed data where the array size was huge and dissecting the array elements didn't properly advance the offset, causing an effectively infinite loop.\n\nFix #19768",
